From 1bfcd24042472101d67c91c0c246ae7da1ef32d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:52:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(coreelec): add CoreELEC ARMHF and ARM64 platforms

Run TizenTube (Cobalt 27) as a Kodi add-on on Amlogic CoreELEC boxes:
CoreELEC NG 32-bit (Mali fbdev) and CE-NO 64-bit (Mali GBM/DRM).

- Platforms evergreen-arm-hardfp-coreelec and evergreen-arm64-coreelec,
  built with the CoreELEC toolchain and sysroot.
- Video: decode in the Amlogic hardware decoder through gst-amlvideosink,
  placed in a hole in the UI; auto frame rate and resolution limits via a
  TizenTube display extension (SetFrameRate).
- Audio: AC3/E-AC3 passthrough to HDMI when Kodi passes them through.
- Widevine L3: an OpenCDM library (ocdm_widevine) that talks to a separate
  Android L3 helper over a socket and shared memory, so compressed samples
  are decrypted and still go to the hardware decoder.
- Host tests: ocdm_widevine/tests/run_tests.sh, tests/run_host_tests.sh;
  tests/gbm_smoke_test.cc runs on the device.

The Android helper binary and its vendor runtime are not part of the tree.
